---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
// iOS is in review, so what this page may claim about iPhone and iPad is decided in ONE file that
// the landing page and the CanJam handout read too. When iOS is approved, flip IOS_STATUS there.
import { ATTUNE, IOS_LIVE } from '../data/attune.js';

const email = 'jamey@warrenlabs.com';
---

<Layout
  title="Support · Warren Labs"
  description={`Help and support for Attune, the headphone voice-matching and preference-tuning app for ${ATTUNE.metaPlatforms}. FAQ, troubleshooting, and how to reach a real person.`}
>
  <Nav variant="home" />
  <section class="sec">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <span class="eyebrow">Support</span>
      <h2>We're here to help.</h2>
      <p class="sec-lede">
        Answers to the most common questions are below. If you don't find what you need,
        email us directly. A real person reads every message.
      </p>

      <p class="contact">
        <a href={`mailto:${email}?subject=Attune%20support`}>{email}</a><span class="muted">. We usually reply within two business days.</span>
      </p>

      <h3>Frequently asked</h3>

      <details>
        <summary>What is Attune?</summary>
        <div class="answer">
          <p>
            Attune plays your music through a different tuning on the headphones you already own,
            and lets you flip back to the original instantly, at exactly the same loudness. You can
            aim at our house voice, at the tonal signature of another headphone, or at your own
            result from a blind listening test.
          </p>
          <p>
            Everything is blind and loudness-matched, on your own music, so you're judging tone
            rather than volume.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>What do I need to run it?</summary>
        <div class="answer">
          {IOS_LIVE ? (
            <p>
              <strong>macOS 12 or later on an Apple Silicon Mac</strong>, or <strong>iOS 16 or
              later</strong> on iPhone and iPad. A pair of headphones and some of your own music is
              all you need.
            </p>
          ) : (
            <p>
              <strong>macOS 12 or later on an Apple Silicon Mac.</strong> The iPhone and iPad
              version is in review at Apple and needs <strong>iOS 16 or later</strong>. A pair of
              headphones and some of your own music is all you need.
            </p>
          )}
          <p>
            A demo track is bundled, so the whole flow works the moment you open it, before you
            load anything.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>How do I get started?</summary>
        <div class="answer">
          <p>
            Pick <strong>your headphone</strong> from the bar at the top, choose what to aim at,
            then flip between <strong>Stock</strong> and <strong>Matched</strong>. Same track, same
            loudness, only the tuning changes. When you're ready, use <strong>Find your sound</strong>
            to tune to your own taste.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Does it work with Spotify or Apple Music?</summary>
        <div class="answer">
          <p>
            Not inside Attune, and no app on macOS or iOS can. Streaming audio is protected end to
            end, so no third-party app is allowed to process it. Attune plays music you own: WAV,
            AIFF, FLAC, ALAC, AAC or MP3.
          </p>
          <p>
            There is a way to get your tuning onto streaming, and it's the better answer anyway.
            With Attune Pro you can export your tuning as a standard AutoEq file and load it onto a
            DSP dongle at <a href="/tune">warrenlabs.com/tune</a>. The dongle applies the EQ at the
            output, so it covers everything the device plays, streaming included, and it follows you
            to your phone. Loading needs a desktop copy of Chrome or Edge.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>How do I use my own music?</summary>
        <div class="answer">
          <p>
            Point Attune at your music folder or pick a single track. Attune only gets
            <strong>read-only</strong> access to the files you choose, and it remembers your folder
            so you don't have to re-pick it every launch.
          </p>
          <p>Your music never leaves your device. See privacy, below.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Is Attune free? What does Pro add?</summary>
        <div class="answer">
          <p>
            Free, permanently, and not a trial: the whole audition flow, both target modes, the ear
            exam, fine tune, importing your own measurements, and one saved sound kept for good. No
            account, no card.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Attune Pro is a single $39 purchase</strong>, no subscription, and it adds two
            things: unlimited saved sounds, and EQ export as a standard AutoEq file so a tuning
            found here can travel to your phone, DAP or dongle. It's a Universal Purchase, so buying
            it on the Mac unlocks it on iPhone and iPad, and the other way round.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Importing your own measurement is free and will not become a paid feature.</strong>
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Whose measurements are these? My headphone isn't listed.</summary>
        <div class="answer">
          <p>
            Ours. Every headphone in Attune was measured here on a miniDSP EARS Pro. Nothing is
            pulled from a public database, and the graph draws the rig's uncertainty rather than
            hiding it. We'd rather ship a handful we can stand behind than thousands we can't, and
            the corpus grows as we measure.
          </p>
          <p>
            If yours isn't there, you have two options that work today.
            <strong>Import your own measurement</strong> in CSV, AutoEq or squig format and Attune
            will voice-match to it exactly as it would to a bundled one: we take the difference
            between the two and correct for it, loudness-matched. That path is free. Or
            <strong>send us the headphone</strong>: we measure it on our rig, publish the result
            either way, and add it. Email us the exact make and model and we'll put it on the list.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Is there an iPhone version?</summary>
        <div class="answer">
          {IOS_LIVE ? (
            <p>
              Yes. Attune is on iPhone and iPad, and Attune Pro is a Universal Purchase, so one $39
              unlock covers Mac and iOS in either direction.
            </p>
          ) : (
            <p>
              Yes, and it's in review at Apple right now. It runs on iPhone and iPad and needs iOS
              16 or later. Attune Pro is a Universal Purchase, so the one $39 unlock covers Mac and
              iOS in either direction, whichever you buy it on.
            </p>
          )}
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Why is the graph empty when I open it?</summary>
        <div class="answer">
          <p>
            Because nothing is selected yet, and that's deliberate. The correction is computed from
            a real measured response, so until Attune knows which headphones you own there's nothing
            honest to draw. Pick your pair from the bar at the top and the graph and the Stock /
            Matched comparison come alive immediately.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Why does Matched sound quieter?</summary>
        <div class="answer">
          <p>
            It doesn't. Both sides are set to the same loudness on purpose, and we measured the
            residual rather than assuming it: 0.04 to 1.0 dB across the headphones we tested.
          </p>
          <p>
            That matching is the whole point of the comparison. Anything even slightly louder sounds
            better for the first few seconds, every time, to everyone. Without level matching you
            aren't comparing tunings, you're just finding out which one is louder. If Matched feels
            quieter, what you're hearing is usually a bass or treble shift, not a level shift.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Does it work with wireless or Bluetooth headphones?</summary>
        <div class="answer">
          <p>
            It will play through them, and you can tune them, but wired is the honest
            recommendation. Bluetooth headphones usually apply their own processing that we can't
            see or account for, so what you'd be correcting is the headphone plus whatever its
            firmware is already doing. Our measurements are of the headphone.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>What about my privacy?</summary>
        <div class="answer">
          <p>
            Attune has <strong>no account, no sign-in, and makes no network requests of any
            kind</strong>. It collects nothing and sends nothing. Your music, your listening and
            your tunings stay on your device. There's nothing to opt out of because there's nothing
            being gathered.
          </p>
          <p>Full details on our <a href="/privacy">privacy page</a>.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>The app won't open, or I can't hear a difference.</summary>
        <div class="answer">
          <p>
            <strong>Won't open:</strong> confirm you're on macOS 12 or later with Apple Silicon, or
            iOS 16 or later, and that Attune came from the App Store. Quit and relaunch. If it still
            won't start, email us your OS version and device model.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>No difference:</strong> check that a headphone is selected, that the correct
            <strong>output device</strong> is chosen inside Attune, and that a track is playing.
            Then remember the Stock and Matched comparison is
            <strong>loudness-matched on purpose</strong>. Listen for a change in <em>tone</em>, not
            a jump in level. Some pairs and some targets are a small correction, and a small
            correction is a small difference.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>What's the demo track?</summary>
        <div class="answer">
          <p>
            "Off Road", written and performed by Jamey Warren and Kevin Toll, &copy; 2021. Jamey is
            a rights holder, which is why it can ship with the app.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>How do refunds work?</summary>
        <div class="answer">
          <p>
            Anything bought through the App Store is handled by Apple. Visit
            <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com">reportaproblem.apple.com</a> to request a refund.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <h3>Reporting a bug</h3>
      <p>The more of this you can include, the faster we can help:</p>
      <ul class="checklist">
        <li>Your <strong>OS version</strong>: Apple menu → About This Mac, or Settings → General → About</li>
        <li>Your <strong>device</strong>: e.g. MacBook Air (M2, 2022), or iPhone 15 Pro</li>
        <li><strong>What you did</strong>: the steps that led to the problem</li>
        <li><strong>What you expected</strong> vs. <strong>what happened</strong></li>
        <li>A screenshot, if it's something you can see</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
  <Footer variant="home" />
</Layout>

<style>
  .prose { max-width: 720px; }
  .prose h3 { margin: 36px 0 10px; font-size: 1.15rem; }
  .prose p { margin: 0 0 14px; line-height: 1.65; }

  .contact { font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .contact .muted { opacity: 0.55; font-size: 0.92rem; }

  .checklist { margin: 6px 0 14px; padding-left: 20px; line-height: 1.75; }
  .checklist li { margin: 0 0 4px; }

  details {
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);
    padding: 13px 0;
  }
  details:last-of-type { border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12); }
  summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    font-weight: 500;
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 16px;
  }
  summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
  summary::after { content: '+'; opacity: 0.55; }
  details[open] summary::after { content: '–'; }
  .answer { margin-top: 10px; opacity: 0.82; }
  .answer p { margin: 0 0 10px; }
  .answer p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
</style>
